      </p>

      <h2>1. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old (or the age of majority where you live) to create an account. Spark is
        designed for parents and caregivers to track habits for children in their care. Children may look at the App's
        kid-facing screens with a grown-up, but may not create or manage an account.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You're responsible for your account and for activity under it, including activity by grown-ups you invite to
        your family. Keep your sign-in methods secure and tell us promptly if you believe your account has been accessed
        without permission. Only add information about children you are a parent, legal guardian, or authorized
        caregiver of.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Family sharing</h2>
      <p>
        With Spark Plus, you can invite other grown-ups to your family using an invite code. Everyone in a family can see
        and change the family's children, habits, check-offs, rewards, and photos. Only share invite codes with people
        you trust. The family owner can remove members. If the owner deletes their account, ownership passes to another
        member and the family's data stays with the remaining members.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Spark Plus subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Spark's core features are free. Spark Plus is an optional subscription that unlocks additional features, such
        as unlimited children and habits, family sharing, full progress history, unlimited reward goals, per-child
        reminder times, photo habit icons, and printable charts. Features may change over time.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plans and price.</strong> Spark Plus is offered as a monthly subscription ($4.99 USD per month) or an
          annual subscription ($39.99 USD per year). Prices may vary by country and are shown in the App before you
          buy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Free trial.</strong> Eligible new subscribers to the annual plan get a 7-day free trial. Unless you
          cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends, you'll be charged for the annual plan when the trial ends.
          Any unused portion of a free trial is forfeited when you purchase a subscription.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment.</strong> Payment is charged to your Apple ID account when you confirm the purchase (or when the
          free trial ends).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automatic renewal.</strong> Your subscription renews automatically for the same period and price
          unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. Your account will be charged for
          renewal within 24 hours before the end of the current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cancelling.</strong> You can manage or cancel your subscription in your App Store account settings
          (Settings → your name → Subscriptions). Deleting the App or your Spark account does not cancel your
          subscription. After you cancel, Plus stays active until the end of the period you've paid for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Refunds.</strong> Purchases are processed by Apple, and refunds are handled by Apple under its
          policies. You can request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Household.</strong> A Spark Plus subscription unlocks Plus features for every grown-up in the
          subscriber's family in the App. If the subscriber leaves the family or the subscription ends, Plus features
          end for the family. Data you created with Plus stays in your account, but some of it may be hidden or
          read-only on the free plan.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Price changes.</strong> If we change the price of Spark Plus, Apple will notify you in advance as
          required, and you can cancel before the new price applies.
        </li>
      </ul>

